# R42 revision 8 — check 16: what verifies a prebuilt artifact before it reaches a
# contributor's PATH? Revision 7 substituted `cargo binstall` for `cargo install --locked`
# on the owner's licence ruling and proved (check 15) that `--locked` binds only the compile
# fallback. This check establishes what, if anything, binds the prebuilt path instead.
#
# Run three times, at 2026-09-13T08:13:31Z, 08:14:05Z and 08:24:35Z, which is 2026-09-13
# 01:13, 01:14 and 01:24 America/Los_Angeles (the stamps are the mtimes of the outputs each
# run captured; the script prints no timestamp of its own). The execution recorded below is
# the FIRST. The second was run only to establish the rerun rule; the THIRD was run after
# this revision was committed, to show the script is still rerunnable from the committed
# tree, and differed from the first in exactly the four lines the rule below names.
#
# Working directory: the run directory. Scratch directory: <scratch>/r42r8run, outside the
# repository. Nothing was installed: the v1.23.0 release asset is unzipped into the scratch
# directory and put on PATH for the duration of the script only, every binstall call carries
# --dry-run, and the listing of ~/.cargo/bin is hashed before and after to show it did not
# change. That listing hashes to 01a2cddcc8ceeb3c17d93fc7bec5d3cbf440ee7416dd81374e4b982acfa389ed,
# the same value check 15 recorded, so this host's tool set is unchanged since that check.
#
# The script below is the complete check. It runs under `set -o pipefail`, tests every
# command's status separately rather than trusting a pipeline, and carries TWO controls that
# make it capable of failing in both directions: a negative control (step 7d, a crate that
# cannot resolve, exit 76) and a POSITIVE control (step 7c, a crate that does declare a
# signing key, which must print exactly one `Verified signature` line). Its User-Agent names
# the repository by URL and carries no personal contact address.
#
# RERUN RULE, stated for both cases.
# (a) On THIS host: byte-for-byte, except four lines. Two consecutive runs differed in exactly
#     these and nothing else:
#       1. `command -v cargo-binstall -> …` — the scratch directory's absolute path.
#       2-4. the three `INFO Done in <elapsed>` lines in steps 7a, 7b and 7c — wall-clock timings.
# (b) On ANY OTHER host: what must match are the exit statuses (0 throughout, and 76 for the
#     negative control), every sha256 of a file fetched at the immutable tag v1.23.0, every
#     source excerpt quoted from those files, the three PRESENT/ABSENT signing verdicts in
#     step 6 (crates.io versions are immutable), the count `7a 'Verified signature'
#     occurrences: 0`, the count `7c 'Verified signature' occurrences: 1`, and the fall-through
#     to `cargo install` under --only-signed in step 7b. These lines carry host or target state
#     and WILL differ:
#       1. the scratch path, $CARGO_HOME and the resolved `cargo` executable inside the
#          `Dry-run: running …` and `- <bin> => …` lines.
#       2. the two `~/.cargo/bin listing sha256` lines — this host's installed tool set. They
#          must equal EACH OTHER on any host; their value is meaningless across hosts.
#       3. the asset name `cargo-binstall-aarch64-apple-darwin.zip` and the downloaded binary's
#          sha256 `5e17743f…` — Darwin/arm64 only. A Linux rerun must fetch the matching asset.
#       4. the target triple inside each WARN line. Note step 7c resolved
#          `(x86_64-apple-darwin)` on this arm64 host, because cargo-binstall's own release
#          maps that target to a `zip` artifact; the signature verification is unaffected and
#          the `Verified signature` line precedes it.
#       5. the `trusted comment` fields inside 7c's `Verified signature` line — `gh=`, `git=`,
#          `ts=` and `run=` are the values cargo-bins' release workflow signed into the
#          artifact for v1.23.0, so they are fixed for that version but would move for another.
#
# WHAT THIS CHECK DOES NOT SHOW. No artifact was installed, so no post-install verification
# was observed. Nothing here measures how many of the tools the template will actually declare
# publish a signing key; the three specs below are the ones check 15 already exercised plus
# cargo-binstall itself. Nothing here was timed.
#
# ---8<--- check16.sh ---8<---
